body:
Godot v4.4.stable.mono - still happening in my project (Update: also Reproducible with the MRP - [bug-thread-improved.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19147185/bug-thread-improved.zip)). I agree that this should be a high priority issue.

Godot v4.4.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900KF (32 threads)

<details>

<summary>Details and Code Example:</summary>

~~On my actual (proprietary) project (where I need to load a large scene via a button), I'm seeing the problem more of the time when not calling `RenderingServer.ForceSync()` at all:
60% of the time ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest is getting stuck at 50% (Stuck: 30 times, Completed Normally: 20 times).~~

~~When calling `RenderingServer.ForceSync()` immediately after each call to `ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus()`, it appears that my odds improve significantly:
12% of the time ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest is getting stuck at 50% (Stuck: 6 times, Completed Normally: 44 times).~~

Edit: I think the difference in odds of getting stuck was just a fluke. If I run tests in one time frame, I might have more or less luck than another time frame. I'm not confident that RenderingServer.ForceSync() is actually helping lower the frequency of the issue.

```
using Godot;

public partial class Main : Node3D
{
    private const string resourcePath = "res://MyLargeScene.tscn";
    private bool isLoading;
    private bool isLoadingStuckMessageLogged;
    private float maxProgress;
    private DateTime startTime;
    private ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus threadLoadStatus = ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus.Failed;

    [Export] Button LoadButton { get; set; }
    [Export] Node3D TargetParent  { get; set; }

    private override void _Ready()
    {
        LoadButton.Pressed += HandleLoadButtonPressed;
    }

    private override void _ExitTree()
    {
        LoadButton.Pressed -= HandleLoadButtonPressed;
    }

    private void HandleLoadButtonPressed()
    {
        if (isLoading)
        {
            return;
        }

        startTime = DateTime.UtcNow;

        isLoading = true;
        GD.Print("Loading: Started");

        var godotError = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest(resourcePath);
        if (godotError != Error.Ok)
        {
            // I have only seen Godot.Error.Ok during testing.
            isLoading = false;
            GD.Print($"ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest returned Godot Error: {godotError}");
        }
    }

    public override void _Process(double delta)
    {
        if (!isLoading)
        {
            return;
        }

        Godot.Collections.Array currentProgressArray = [];
        var currentThreadLoadStatus = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus(resourcePath, currentProgressArray);
        RenderingServer.ForceSync(); // Decreases the odds of ResourceLoader getting stuck in my testing.
        var currentProgress = currentProgressArray[0].AsSingle();

        if (currentProgress > maxProgress)
        {
            maxProgress = currentProgress;
            GD.Print($"Loading: {currentProgress * 100}%");
        }

        if (currentThreadLoadStatus != threadLoadStatus)
        {
            threadLoadStatus = currentThreadLoadStatus;
            GD.Print($"Loading: ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus {threadLoadStatus}");

            if (threadLoadStatus == ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus.Loaded)
            {
                Complete();
            }
        }

        var realTimeElapsed = DateTime.UtcNow - startTime;
        if (realTimeElapsed.TotalSeconds > 3.0f && !isLoadingStuckMessageLogged)
        {
            GD.Print("Loading: Incomplete after 3s, ResourceLoader may have gotten stuck. Please restart. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99128 for details on the issue.");
            isLoadingStuckMessageLogged = true;
        }
    }

    private void Complete()
    {
        var resource = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGet(resourcePath);
        var packedScene = resource as PackedScene;
        var node = packedScene?.Instantiate() ?? null;
        isLoading = false;

        if (node is null)
        {
            GD.Print("Loading: Failed");
        }
        else
        {
            GD.Print("Loading: Completed");
            TargetParent.AddChild(node);
        }
    }
}
```

</details>

I stumbled upon a clue or a possible fix. I can load consistently after moving `CreateScriptBridgeForType` out of the upgradeable read lock in `ScriptManagerBridge.GetOrCreateScriptBridgeForType` like so:

```cs
private static unsafe void GetOrCreateScriptBridgeForType(Type scriptType, godot_ref* outScript)
{
    _scriptTypeBiMap.ReadWriteLock.EnterUpgradeableReadLock();
    try
    {
        if (_scriptTypeBiMap.TryGetScriptPtr(scriptType, out IntPtr scriptPtr))
        {
            // Use existing
            NativeFuncs.godotsharp_ref_new_from_ref_counted_ptr(out *outScript, scriptPtr);
            return;
        }
    }
    finally
    {
        _scriptTypeBiMap.ReadWriteLock.ExitUpgradeableReadLock();
    }
    // This path is slower, but it's only executed for the first instantiation of the type
    CreateScriptBridgeForType(scriptType, outScript);
}
```
Edit made on commit 80a3d205f1ad22e779a64921fb56d62b893881ae

This may introduce a race condition between exiting the upgradeable lock and entering the write lock in `CreateScriptBridgeForType` and I am unsure if `NativeFuncs.godotsharp_internal_reload_registered_script` in `CreateScriptBridgeForType` needs to be in a lock.

@TCROC I believe he "fixed" it using a similar approach in [this pull request](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798). However, that PR wasn't merged because the Godot team chose to proceed with [this alternative PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99539), which unfortunately does not resolve the issue.

So we still have the problem. The approach he mentioned was considered risk by the godot team, please refer to the first PR mentioned.

Event after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99539 I still can reproduce it.

As a temporary workaround while this gets patched, in C# you can do: 
```csharp
await Task.Run(() =>
	{
		ResourceLoader.Load("res://Your/resource.res", cacheMode: ResourceLoader.CacheMode.Reuse);
	}
);
```
Once at game startup to cache it in advance without blocking the main thread. Subsequent loads start at 0.81 and don't get stuck in an infinite loop.

If the closed PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798) fixes the issue you all are getting and doesn't introduce other issues, then we can reopen it and merge it. It was closed because we didn't have enough confidence it wouldn't introduce other bugs, and it initially seemed the alternative PR would fix this bug too.

@TCROC Did you end up testing https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798? If so, did that PR fix the issue for you?

@dougVanny You said you are unable to compile Godot, would you be willing to test a custom build that includes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798? If so, what platform does the editor need to target? And if you need to test this in an exported game, what platforms do the templates need to target?

In general, the more people test and confirm that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798 fixes the issue without introducing other issues, the more confident we'll be to merge the PR. I'm currently unable to reproduce this issue, so testing and reviews from other users and contributors is much appreciated.
